@@ -17,3 +17,17 @@ make demo-data  # load sample rows for local browsing
 ```
 
 The API listens on the port given by `PORT`, default 3000.
+
+## Booking rules
+
+A booking request is refused when:
+
+- `endsAt` is not strictly after `startsAt` (400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`).
+- `startsAt` or `endsAt` is not an ISO-8601 instant (400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`).
+- the room or the user does not exist (404 `NOT_FOUND`).
+- the period overlaps another active booking of the same room (409
+  `BOOKING_CONFLICT`, with the offending booking in `details`).
+
+Periods are half-open: a booking that starts exactly when another ends is
+accepted. Cancelled bookings release their slot. `PATCH /bookings/:id`
+applies the same rules to the period that results from the change.
